{
  "description": "R2: few-shot dose x DIV trajectory forecasting on unseen chemicals (EPA NFA), 5-fold chemical CV.",
  "protocol": "R2: few-shot dose x DIV trajectory forecasting on unseen chemicals (EPA NFA), 5-fold chemical CV.\n\nProtocol (fixed before evaluation):\n- Outer folds: repo/results/splits_epa_nfa.json (all SPIDs of a chemical in one fold).\n- For each held-out chemical and k in {0,1,2,3,4} measured concentration levels, the context is\n  every well at k levels (5 seeded designs per k) and the targets are all wells at the other levels.\n  Every method receives exactly the same context.\n- Primary metric, CURVE MAE: for each held-out level, |prediction - mean of its replicate wells|\n  over the observed (DIV, feature) entries; averaged per chemical, then over chemicals.\n  Secondary metric, WELL MAE: the same against every individual well (dominated by replicate noise).\n- Model selection is nested: inside each outer training set, one inner fold is held out to choose\n  the likelihood (gaussian | laplace), the number of steps and the decoder (plain | interpolation-informed); the chosen configuration is then\n  retrained on the whole outer training set with 3 seeds (ensemble). Outer test chemicals are never\n  used for any choice.\n- Uncertainty: paired bootstrap over chemicals of (NeuroTrajectory - baseline).\n\nUsage: python repo/scripts/run_trajectory_cv.py [--seeds 0 1 2] [--quick]",
  "n_chemicals": 49,
  "outer_folds": [
    0
  ],
  "seeds": [
    0
  ],
  "designs_per_k": 5,
  "nested_selection": {
    "0": {
      "note": "smoke test, no nesting"
    }
  },
  "development_note": "During development one smoke run (800 steps, 1 seed) was evaluated on outer fold 0 and motivated adding the interpolation-informed decoder as a candidate; the final choice is nested. 'by_k_folds_1to4' excludes fold 0 entirely.",
  "target_units": "asinh(x/c_f) minus plate/date/DIV vehicle median, divided by pooled within-plate vehicle robust SD; clipped to +-10",
